claim.claim-text:
a dry-type transformer including first (102), second (104) and third windings (106),
a first surge arrester (120);
a second surge arrester (122);
the first surge arrester(120) and the second surge arrester (122) being series-connected with each other and parallel-connected with the first winding (102), wherein a connection point between the first surge arrester (120) and the second surge arrester (122) is electrically connected to a location of the first winding (102);
a third surge arrester (128);
a fourth surge arrester (130);
the third surge arrester (128) and the fourth surge arrester (130) being series-connected with each other and parallel connected with the second winding (104), wherein a connection point between the third surge arrester (128) and the fourth surge arrester (130) is electrically connected to a location of the second winding;
a fifth surge arrester (134); and
a sixth surge arrester (136);
the fifth surge arrester (134) and the sixth surge arrester (136) being series-connected with each other and parallel-connected with the third winding (106), wherein a connection point between the fifth surge arrester (134) and the sixth surge arrester (136) is electrically connected to a location of the third winding (106),
wherein each of the first, second and third windings (102, 104, 106) have first and second ends and the distance from the first end to the second end is length (L), wherein the respective connection point is the middle location of the first, second and third windings (102, 104, 106), which is located in a range of from L/4 to 3(L/4),
wherein the first (102), second (104) and third windings (106) are interconnected in a configuration of a Y-connected transformer,
the system (100) further comprising:

a seventh surge arrester (114) having fist and second ends, the first end of the seventh surge arrester (114) electrically connected to the first end of the first winding (102);
a eighth surge arrester (116) having fist and second ends, the first end of the eighth surge arrester (116) electrically connected to the first end of the second winding (104); and
a ninth surge arrester (118) having fist and second ends, the first end of the ninth surge arrester (118) electrically connected to the first end of the third winding (106);
wherein the second ends of said seventh (114), eighth (116) and ninth surge arresters (118) are each electrically connected to ground.

a first capacitor (140) electrically connected in parallel with said seventh surge arrester (114);
a second capacitor (142) electrically connected in parallel with said eighth surge arrester (116); and
a third capacitor (144) electrically connected in parallel with said ninth surge arrester (118).

said first surge arrestor comprises two series-connected surge arrestors 1-1 and 1-2;
said second surge arrestor comprises two series-connected surge arrestors 2-1 and 2-2;
wherein surge arrestor 1-1 has a first end electrically connected to the first end of the first winding (102) and surge arrestor 1-2 has a second end electrically connected to the middle location of the first winding (102);
said surge arrestor 1-1 has a second end electrically connected to a first end of surge arrestor 1-2 and to a location along the first winding (102) between the first end and the middle location;
wherein surge arrestor 2-2 has a second end electrically connected to the second end of the first winding (102) and surge arrestor 2-1 has a first end electrically connected to the middle location of the first winding (102);
said surge arrestor 2-1 has a second end electrically connected to a first end of surge arrestor 2-2 and to a location along the first winding (102) between the second end and the middle location.

said third surge arrestor comprises two series-connected surge arrestors 3-1 and 3-2;
said fourth surge arrestor comprises two series-connected surge arrestors 4-1 and 4-2;
wherein surge arrestor 3-1 has a first end electrically connected to the first end of the second winding (104) and surge arrestor 3-2 has a second end electrically connected to the middle location of the second winding (104);
said surge arrestor 3-1 has a second end electrically connected to a first end of surge arrestor 3-2 and to a location along the second winding (104) between the first end and the middle location;
wherein surge arrestor 4-2 has a second end electrically connected to the second end of the second winding (104) and surge arrestor 4-1 has a first end electrically connected to the middle location of the second winding (104);
said surge arrestor 4-1 has a second end electrically connected to a first end of surge arrestor 4-2 and to a location along the second winding (104) between the second end and the middle location.

said fifth surge arrestor comprises two series-connected surge arrestors 5-1 and 5-2;
said sixth surge arrestor comprises two series-connected surge arrestors 6-1 and 6-2;
wherein surge arrestor 5-1 has a first end electrically connected to the first end of the third winding (106) and surge arrestor 5-2 has a second end electrically connected to the middle location of the third winding (106);
said surge arrestor 5-1 has a second end electrically connected to a first end of surge arrestor 5-2 and to a location along the third winding (106) between the first end and the middle location;
wherein surge arrestor 6-2 has a second end electrically connected to the second end of the third winding (106) and surge arrestor 6-1 has a first end electrically connected to the middle location of the third winding (106);
said surge arrestor 6-1 has a second end electrically connected to a first end of surge arrestor 6-2 and to a location along the third winding (106) between the second end and the middle location.
